+# Fooocus + Snapdragon NPU
+
+Run Stable Diffusion on the Hexagon NPU while keeping Fooocus's web UI for
+prompting, queueing and the gallery.
+
+## Backends
+
+| Backend | Model | Resolution | Measured |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `sdxl` (default) | DreamShaper XL Lightning, w8a16, 5-part UNet | 1024×1024 | ~2.0 s/step; ~22 s for 8 steps |
+| `sd21` | Qualcomm AI Hub SD 2.1, w8a16 | 512×512 | ~0.36 s/step; ~3 s for 8 steps |
+| SDXL inpaint | same UNet + QNN VAE encoder, masked-latent blending | 1024×1024 | ~20–30 s for 8 steps, warm |
+
+The backend is auto-detected from the model directory: a `metadata.json` +
+single-graph `text_encoder.onnx` means SD 2.1; `unet_w8a16_quantized/` or
+`unet/` directories mean SDXL.
+
+## Architecture
+
+- The NPU only works from an **ARM64 Python** (QNN ships ARM64 DLLs), so the
+  engine runs as a separate process (`npu/server.py`, `qnn_env`, port 7867).
+  Fooocus (x64) talks to it over HTTP and streams NDJSON progress + PNGs.
+- `modules/npu_bridge.py` hooks `modules/async_worker.py::handler()`: with
+  `FOOOCUS_NPU=1` generation is routed to the NPU and the PyTorch SDXL
+  pipeline is skipped.
+- The torch SDXL pipeline is imported lazily. NPU text-to-image never loads the
+  checkpoint, so the UI process stays near 1 GB instead of ~16 GB. The import
+  happens on the first task that falls through to the CPU pipeline.
+- The sampler/scheduler stays host-side (numpy); only text encoders, UNet and
+  VAE run on the NPU.
+
+## Assets
+
+SDXL (community precompiled QNN, MIT):
+`https://huggingface.co/Buuta/dreamshaper-xl-lightning-for-Snapdragon-X-Elite`
+
+Downloaded to `..\sd_xl_npu`:
+
+```
+text_encoder/            CLIP-L (237 MB)
+text_encoder_2/          CLIP-G (1.3 GB)
+tokenizer/ tokenizer_2/  HuggingFace CLIP tokenizers
+unet_w8a16_quantized/    5 parts (2.5 GB)
+vae_decoder/1024x1024/   VAE decoder (162 MB)
+```
+
+SD 2.1 (Qualcomm AI Hub):
+`..\sd21_model\stable_diffusion_v2_1-precompiled_qnn_onnx-w8a16-qualcomm_snapdragon_x_elite`
+
+Only 1024×1024 is available for SDXL until the weight-shared portrait/landscape
+UNet + VAE variants are downloaded.
+
+Inpainting also needs the QNN VAE encoder:
+
+```
+vae_encoder/1024x1024/model.onnx   (98 MB, from the same HuggingFace repo)
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```powershell
+$Work = Join-Path (Get-Location).Path 'fooocus-snapdragon-npu-experiment'
+cd "$Work\Fooocus"
+# FOOOCUS_NPU is optional: launch.py enables the NPU when qnn_env and
+# sd_xl_npu are present. Set FOOOCUS_NPU=0 to force the CPU pipeline.
+$env:no_proxy = "127.0.0.1"
+.\fooocus_env\Scripts\python.exe launch.py --always-cpu --listen 127.0.0.1 --port 7865
+```
+
+The first generation auto-spawns the NPU server (log: `npu/server_7867.log`).
+Fooocus's Performance/steps are clamped for Lightning: steps ≤ 8, CFG ≤ 2.5.
+Aspect ratios other than 1024×1024 fall back to 1024×1024.
+
+## Environment variables
+
+| Variable | Default |
+|---|---|
+| `FOOOCUS_NPU` | auto: on when `qnn_env` and `sd_xl_npu` exist; `0` forces the CPU pipeline |
+| `FOOOCUS_NPU_MODEL` | `..\sd_xl_npu` (SDXL) |
+| `FOOOCUS_NPU_PYTHON` | `..\qnn_env\Scripts\python.exe` |
+| `FOOOCUS_NPU_SERVER` | `npu/server.py` |
+| `FOOOCUS_NPU_HOST` / `FOOOCUS_NPU_PORT` | `127.0.0.1` / `7867` |
+
+Run the server manually:
+
+```powershell
+..\qnn_env\Scripts\python.exe npu\server.py --model-dir ..\sd_xl_npu --port 7867
+..\qnn_env\Scripts\python.exe npu\server.py --model-dir ..\sd21_model\... --port 7868
+```
+
+## Files
+
+- `npu/qnn_sdxl.py` — SDXL wrapper (vendored pipeline + capture of the decoded image)
+- `npu/sdxl/` — vendored SDXL QNN pipeline (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 buuta-buta-butaata)
+- `npu/qnn_sd21.py` — SD 2.1 pipeline (AI Hub graphs)
+- `npu/server.py` — ARM64 HTTP server, backend auto-detection
+- `npu/client.py` — x64 client, auto-spawn, streaming
+- `modules/npu_bridge.py` — Fooocus integration
+
+## Inpainting (NPU)
+
+The Inpaint tab and outpaint run on the NPU:
+
+1. `async_worker` hands `inpaint_image` / `inpaint_mask` to
+   `npu_bridge.run_inpaint_task()`.
+2. The bridge prepares the region with `InpaintWorker` (crop/fill/mask), skipping
+   its ESRGAN pre-upscale (minutes on CPU), and POSTs `/inpaint`.
+3. The server encodes the fill with the QNN VAE encoder, runs the 5-part UNet with
+   masked-latent blending, and decodes with the QNN VAE decoder.
+4. The bridge composites the result back with `InpaintWorker.post_process()`
+   and saves through Fooocus's logger.
+
+Notes:
+
+- This is Fooocus's **non-parameterized inpaint** (masked-latent blending): the
+  Fooocus inpaint head (v2.5/v2.6 patch) cannot be applied to the compiled graph,
+  so quality for large masked areas is below the CPU parameterized path.
+- Denoise strength is honored by slicing the sigma schedule like
+  `KSampler.set_steps`.
+- Steps are clamped to 8 and CFG to 2.0 (Lightning defaults).
+- Enhance tabs (multi-mask flows) and upscale still use the CPU pipeline.
+
+## Assist models (step 4)
+
+The server also exposes two plain-ONNX endpoints, used by Fooocus when
+`FOOOCUS_NPU=1`. They run on QNN when the graph compiles, otherwise on native
+ARM64 CPU (still much faster than the x64-emulated Fooocus process):
+
+| Endpoint | Model | Fooocus wiring |
+|---|---|---|
+| `POST /tagger` | WD14 `wd-v1-4-moat-tagger-v2.onnx` | `extras/wd14tagger.py` (Interrogate) |
+| `POST /mask` | U2Net family (`u2net`, `u2netp`, `u2net_human_seg`, `silueta`) | `extras/inpaint_mask.py` |
+
+Model files (shared with Fooocus's model dirs):
+
+```
+Fooocus\models\clip_vision\wd-v1-4-moat-tagger-v2.onnx   (311 MB)
+Fooocus\models\clip_vision\wd-v1-4-moat-tagger-v2.csv
+Fooocus\models\inpaint\u2net.onnx                         (168 MB)
+```
+
+If a model is missing, Fooocus falls back to its local `onnxruntime`/`rembg`
+path (which downloads it on first use).
+
+## Non-txt2img tasks
+
+`modules/npu_bridge.py::supports_task()` only routes plain text-to-image to the
+NPU. Inpaint, enhance and upscale tasks fall through to the CPU PyTorch pipeline
+(slow but correct) instead of producing a wrong txt2img image.
+
+## Limitations
+
+- SDXL: LoRA/refiner/ControlNet/IP-Adapter/enhance/upscale are not wired to the
+  NPU backend.
+- Inpaint uses masked-latent blending without the Fooocus inpaint head; large
+  masked regions are lower quality than the CPU v2.6 path.
+- SD 2.1: 512×512 fixed, weak text conditioning vs SDXL.
+- QNN graphs are shape-specialized; other aspect ratios need precompiled
+  weight-shared variants.
+- Assist models are single-graph ONNX: QNN may reject some ops, in which case the
+  server logs a warning and runs that model on native ARM64 CPU.
